  "methodology": {
    "benchmark": "Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index plus independently measured API output speed and time to first token. The Intelligence Index is a broad composite benchmark, not a universal definition of model quality; reasoning-effort variants are treated as distinct configurations.",
    "pricing": "First-party standard API list prices are used for the current date. Tool/search/grounding charges, cache writes, volume discounts, batch pricing and premium service tiers are excluded. Announced future prices are encoded when available.",
    "workload": "Scenario cost uses editable input and output token counts: cost = input_tokens × input_rate / 1e6 + output_tokens × output_rate / 1e6. It does not attempt to estimate hidden reasoning-token usage unless the provider bills those tokens as output and they are present in the supplied output-token count.",
    "frontier": "A model is on the displayed price/intelligence frontier when no other scored model has both an equal-or-higher Intelligence Index and an equal-or-lower scenario cost, with at least one strict improvement.",
    "comparability": "Speed and TTFT are observed API measurements and can change with provider load, prompt shape, region and service tier. Benchmark scores can also move when evaluation methodology or model serving changes. Use this explorer to narrow choices, then validate on your own workload."
  },
